## Why This Is Asked
Tests augmented BST design for duplicates and range queries on a dynamic multiset, focusing on balance, memory, and correctness.

## Key Concepts
- Treap with duplicates via per-node cnt
- Subtree size and sum augmentation
- kth smallest by counts; range queries via splits or traversal

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node{constructor(key,prio){this.key=key;this.prio=prio;this.cnt=1;this.l=null;this.r=null;this.sz=1;this.sum=key}};
function upd(n){if(!n)return; n.sz=n.cnt+(n.l?.sz||0)+(n.r?.sz||0); n.sum=n.key*n.cnt+(n.l?.sum||0)+(n.r?.sum||0)}
function rotateRight(y){const x=y.l; y.l=x.r; x.r=y; upd(y); upd(x); return x}
function rotateLeft(x){const y=x.r; x.r=y.l; y.l=x; upd(x); upd(y); return y}
function insert(n, key){if(!n)return new Node(key,Math.random()); if(key===n.key){n.cnt++; upd(n);return n}; if(key<n.key){n.l=insert(n.l,key); if(n.l.prio>n.prio) n=rotateRight(n);} else {n.r=insert(n.r,key); if(n.r.prio>n.prio) n=rotateLeft(n);} upd(n); return n}
function kth(n,k){if(!n) return null; const leftSize=n.l?.sz||0; if(k<=leftSize) return kth(n.l,k); if(k>leftSize+n.cnt) return kth(n.r,k-leftSize-n.cnt); return n.key;}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a dynamic, frequency-based data structure for text streams, common in search, analytics, and logs.

## Key Concepts
- Dual-map design: word→freq and freq→ordered words
- Efficient updates by relocating words between buckets
- Tie-breaking by lexicographic order
- Corner cases: zero counts, topK when fewer distinct words

## Code Example
```javascript
class WordFreqDS {
  constructor() {
    this.counts = new Map();
    this.buckets = new Map(); // freq -> Set<string>
  }
  _ensureBucket(freq) {
    if (!this.buckets.has(freq)) this.buckets.set(freq, new Set());
  }
  addWord(word) {
    const prev = this.counts.get(word) || 0;
    if (prev > 0) this.buckets.get(prev).delete(word);
    const next = prev + 1;
    this.counts.set(word, next);
    this._ensureBucket(next);
    this.buckets.get(next).add(word);
  }
  eraseWord(word) {
    const prev = this.counts.get(word);
    if (!prev) return;
    this.buckets.get(prev).delete(word);
    const next = prev - 1;
    if (next === 0) {
      this.counts.delete(word);
      return;
    }
    this.counts.set(word, next);
    this._ensureBucket(next);
    this.buckets.get(next).add(word);
  }
  getFrequency(word) {
    return this.counts.get(word) || 0;
  }
  topKWords(n) {
    const freqs = Array.from(this.buckets.keys()).sort((a,b)=>b-a);
    const res = [];
    for (const freq of freqs) {
      const words = Array.from(this.buckets.get(freq)).sort();
      for (const w of words) {
        res.push(w);
        if (res.length === n) return res;
      }
    }
    return res;
  }
}
```

